WEBVTT

00:33.750 --> 00:36.250
Okay, Mr. Fisher. I'll give you a minute.

00:43.916 --> 00:45.041
God.

00:54.875 --> 00:56.166
My boy.

01:13.666 --> 01:15.582
Here. Clean yourself up.

01:15.583 --> 01:17.374
Yeah, where's my son?

01:17.375 --> 01:21.832
You think you get to make demands
after holding my daughter hostage?

01:21.833 --> 01:23.874
I should put a bullet in your head!

01:23.875 --> 01:25.875
That's tough talk for a man
that kidnaps kids.

01:27.291 --> 01:28.375
Get him up.

01:38.208 --> 01:40.375
So what's happening? Where's Matthew?

01:41.541 --> 01:42.625
I don't know.

01:44.291 --> 01:47.500
I swear to God, if I did,
I'd go get him with you.

01:49.250 --> 01:51.040
Yeah, sure you would.

01:51.041 --> 01:53.041
Whatever he wants to talk about,

01:53.958 --> 01:55.833
you gotta ask yourself why.

01:57.291 --> 02:00.166
He's always got an endgame,
and it's never what you think.

02:06.375 --> 02:07.625
Look familiar?

02:09.291 --> 02:10.665
Yeah, it's Revere Boardwalk.

02:10.666 --> 02:12.833
Yeah, right down
to the Revere Diner there.

02:14.166 --> 02:16.665
Yeah, it took me years
to put this together.

02:16.666 --> 02:20.290
Brought stuff in from Atlantic City,
Coney Island.

02:20.291 --> 02:23.458
Got the merry-go-round
from Venice Beach, California.

02:24.625 --> 02:26.458
Know why I built all this?

02:28.375 --> 02:29.333
No.

02:29.916 --> 02:33.874
When my son, Liam, was little, we used
to go to the boardwalk every weekend.

02:33.875 --> 02:35.250
It was his favorite place.

02:36.416 --> 02:39.000
Liam has been dead
more than ten years now.

02:40.916 --> 02:42.375
Every time I come here,

02:43.583 --> 02:45.041
my memories of him,

02:45.791 --> 02:47.166
our time together,

02:48.375 --> 02:50.666
it's fresh as the salt in the air.

02:51.791 --> 02:53.541
That's why I brought you here.

02:54.916 --> 02:56.041
Both of you.

03:09.916 --> 03:13.375
Oh, whoa. It's okay.
Let him up. It's all right.

03:27.250 --> 03:28.332
You okay?

03:28.333 --> 03:29.250
I'm fine.

03:30.375 --> 03:31.583
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

03:32.083 --> 03:33.499
- Okay.
- Let's sit.

03:33.500 --> 03:34.500
Yeah.

03:39.791 --> 03:43.625
You know, your old man and me,
we go way back.

03:44.291 --> 03:46.875
We both made our bones
in the neighborhood.

03:47.833 --> 03:51.250
Yeah, opposite sides of the street,
so to speak, but, uh…

03:51.750 --> 03:54.000
Simpler times, wasn't it, Lenny?

03:55.583 --> 03:57.207
- Was he a good father?
- Nicky.

03:57.208 --> 04:00.791
Yeah, I'm just asking a question.
Was he a good father?

04:01.666 --> 04:02.500
Yeah.

04:03.083 --> 04:04.291
Look up to him?

04:05.125 --> 04:08.416
Yeah, of course you did.
Sons look up to their fathers.

04:09.208 --> 04:11.416
Doesn't matter who they are
or what they did.

04:12.041 --> 04:14.290
We get to be their first heroes.

04:14.291 --> 04:16.624
There's nothing like it.
Nothing can replace it.

04:16.625 --> 04:19.333
Nicky, what the hell's this about?

04:21.208 --> 04:25.332
Are you really gonna sit there
and pretend that you don't know? Hmm?

04:25.333 --> 04:26.540
Okay, just…

04:26.541 --> 04:28.124
Easy, easy.

04:28.125 --> 04:29.582
Just tell me what you want.

04:29.583 --> 04:31.875
I want my son back.

04:33.083 --> 04:35.291
But that's not possible, is it, Lenny?

04:37.250 --> 04:38.166
Nah.

04:38.833 --> 04:42.166
You see, ten years ago,
Liam got himself into a bar fight.

04:43.208 --> 04:46.291
Some idiot was running his mouth,
and that idiot ended up dead.

04:48.458 --> 04:50.750
But my son had his whole life
ahead of him.

04:51.666 --> 04:54.249
There were about a dozen people
that saw what went down.

04:54.250 --> 04:56.832
But here's the funny thing
about witnesses,

04:56.833 --> 05:00.708
their memories get foggy
if you give them the right incentive.

05:02.416 --> 05:05.000
The DA was ready to drop all charges.

05:06.875 --> 05:10.208
And then these two detectives
show up out of nowhere.

05:11.166 --> 05:15.083
And they decide that my son
needs to pay for what he did.

05:16.000 --> 05:18.415
They manufacture evidence,

05:18.416 --> 05:20.875
and that sends him
to Massachusetts Correctional…

05:22.958 --> 05:24.540
…where he is murdered.

05:24.541 --> 05:25.665
Your son killed that boy.

05:25.666 --> 05:28.040
My son died in the dirt
like a fucking animal

05:28.041 --> 05:29.791
because of you and Phil Mackenzie.

05:32.250 --> 05:35.290
So now, David, you tell me,

05:35.291 --> 05:37.750
what would you do to save your son?

05:39.416 --> 05:41.291
What are you willing to sacrifice?

05:42.041 --> 05:43.208
Anything.

05:43.791 --> 05:45.333
Well, let's find out.

05:48.708 --> 05:51.875
Life of your father
for that of your little boy.

06:14.708 --> 06:16.000
Ah!

06:17.583 --> 06:19.124
I need EMPs here now!

06:19.125 --> 06:19.958
Sarah.

06:20.666 --> 06:21.708
Sarah!

06:24.041 --> 06:25.041
Hey.

06:25.541 --> 06:26.916
How are you holding up?

06:28.291 --> 06:29.541
I'm fine.

06:30.458 --> 06:33.541
They were able to get
his blood pressure up to finish surgery.

06:34.750 --> 06:36.915
He's not out of the woods yet,
but he's stable.

06:36.916 --> 06:38.291
Oh, I'm glad to hear it.

06:39.625 --> 06:41.707
Were they able to find the plane
Burroughs was on?

06:41.708 --> 06:44.290
We ran the tail number,
pulled the flight plan,

06:44.291 --> 06:47.790
had agents waiting at the tarmac
when Nicky's plane landed in Miami,

06:47.791 --> 06:50.040
but it was empty.

06:50.041 --> 06:53.000
You were expecting Nicky Fisher
to follow a flight plan?

06:53.541 --> 06:56.457
We need to call
every private airport in Florida.

06:56.458 --> 06:59.541
- They had to let them out somewhere.
- We are looking into it.

07:01.125 --> 07:02.166
Hold on…

07:06.666 --> 07:07.707
You're benching me.

07:07.708 --> 07:09.290
No one is benching you.

07:09.291 --> 07:12.332
Your partner was shot.
You know the protocol.

07:12.333 --> 07:13.790
My father almost died,

07:13.791 --> 07:15.582
and you want to talk to me about protocol.

07:15.583 --> 07:19.332
This is why the Bureau doesn't normally
allow families to work together.

07:19.333 --> 07:20.457
This, right here.

07:20.458 --> 07:23.874
Max pulled strings
so that you could be his partner.

07:23.875 --> 07:27.125
Not his daughter, his partner.
So you need to act like it.

07:27.791 --> 07:28.708
Go home.

07:29.208 --> 07:31.875
Clean up, so you can be here
when he wakes up.

07:49.708 --> 07:51.082
Agent Greer.

07:51.083 --> 07:53.791
This is Detective Daniel Müller
with the Swiss police.

07:54.416 --> 07:58.332
I received your Interpol request.
I'll be arriving in Boston tomorrow.

07:58.333 --> 07:59.957
I need to speak to you.

07:59.958 --> 08:03.916
I have important information
about the Matthew Burroughs case.

08:09.333 --> 08:11.541
If you want to see your son again,

08:12.125 --> 08:14.125
you have to make the choice, David.

08:15.791 --> 08:17.332
Nicky, what the fuck?

08:17.333 --> 08:18.624
This doesn't concern you.

08:18.625 --> 08:20.166
Of course it does. We have a deal.

08:20.750 --> 08:21.750
What deal?

08:22.958 --> 08:27.415
I put a hit out on your father
and Mackenzie after Liam was killed.

08:27.416 --> 08:31.250
And then this guy shows up
at my door with a proposition.

08:32.000 --> 08:36.041
I spare their lives,
and he's my guy inside BPD.

08:39.583 --> 08:42.249
And that was a hard decision,
letting you live.

08:42.250 --> 08:46.708
But one I had to make peace with.
Now, make your choice, David.

08:49.916 --> 08:51.499
I'm not…

08:51.500 --> 08:53.374
I can't… I won't do this.

08:53.375 --> 08:55.666
Then I guess I have my answer.
Kill them both.

08:56.583 --> 08:58.250
Put your weapon down now!

08:59.958 --> 09:02.375
I will shoot you, so help me God.

09:02.958 --> 09:05.082
Well, I guess you just
can't buy loyalty, huh?

09:05.083 --> 09:07.124
This doesn't have to go down this way.

09:07.125 --> 09:08.250
Yeah.

09:08.916 --> 09:11.875
David, you said you'd do anything.

09:12.500 --> 09:13.666
Anything!

09:14.333 --> 09:15.749
I can't do this.

09:15.750 --> 09:17.915
Wait, David, listen to me.

09:17.916 --> 09:20.499
- This is easy. Easy decision.
- No.

09:20.500 --> 09:23.125
Look, I'm not gonna survive the cancer.

09:24.750 --> 09:27.833
This way, I go out on my terms.

09:28.458 --> 09:30.208
And more than that,

09:31.458 --> 09:33.333
I get a chance to make this right.

09:35.208 --> 09:38.333
Oh, now that… that is touching.

09:39.291 --> 09:41.790
But it's gotta be his decision, Lenny.

09:41.791 --> 09:43.916
I gotta hear him say it.

09:47.458 --> 09:51.041
Come on. David, come on. You gotta do it.

09:54.125 --> 09:55.333
What's it gonna be?

09:57.791 --> 09:58.750
Come on.

10:02.291 --> 10:03.291
Okay.

10:05.500 --> 10:06.500
Okay.

10:08.625 --> 10:09.625
Okay.

10:13.291 --> 10:15.749
Tell Matthew his glove is at the house.

10:15.750 --> 10:17.166
He's gotta practice.

10:18.291 --> 10:20.333
Sox have a first base problem.

10:29.458 --> 10:32.333
You can put that away, son. It's over.

10:33.916 --> 10:36.665
Sorry, David. I had to be sure.

10:36.666 --> 10:37.708
About what?

10:38.291 --> 10:42.040
That you were innocent,
and that your kid is still alive.

10:42.041 --> 10:44.707
If you were willing
to let your old man die,

10:44.708 --> 10:46.582
then you must be telling the truth.

10:46.583 --> 10:48.166
You don't have him.

10:48.750 --> 10:51.166
I do not kidnap kids.

10:55.125 --> 10:58.791
Charlie 6-1, I'm outside
Rachel Mills's residence. All clear.

11:06.750 --> 11:07.750
Wait a minute.

11:18.250 --> 11:20.041
Is this Davidson Photography?

11:21.083 --> 11:23.665
Great. You shot at a corporate event
at Six Flags a few weeks ago

11:23.666 --> 11:24.999
for the Payne Foundation.

11:25.000 --> 11:27.707
I was sent all your photos,
but I'm missing three.

11:27.708 --> 11:29.958
and I'm wondering
if you could email them to me.

11:31.541 --> 11:32.500
Great.

11:33.083 --> 11:37.125
Uh, it's 110, 111, and 112.

11:37.666 --> 11:40.415
And RMills@Quincy.edu.

11:40.416 --> 11:41.708
Thanks so much.

11:46.083 --> 11:48.249
What a nice surprise. Come in.

11:48.250 --> 11:49.208
Hey.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.416
I stopped by Torretta's.

11:52.000 --> 11:53.625
- Got you a Danish.
- Wow.

11:55.208 --> 11:56.999
What'd I do to deserve this honor?

11:57.000 --> 11:59.124
You know there's a cop
parked outside, right?

11:59.125 --> 12:02.750
They're looking for David.
I haven't seen him since yesterday.

12:03.375 --> 12:05.582
I'm guessing I shouldn't ask about Ronald?

12:05.583 --> 12:07.041
Definitely not.

12:07.958 --> 12:10.041
He's offered to stay at his sister's.

12:15.500 --> 12:17.041
I can't stop looking at this.

12:18.458 --> 12:19.333
I mean, it…

12:20.208 --> 12:23.125
I keep telling myself,
it can't be him, right? It's impossible.

12:26.083 --> 12:27.500
But I know his face.

12:29.833 --> 12:32.040
But I don't understand.

12:32.041 --> 12:35.541
The medical examiner confirmed
it was him in the bed that night.

12:36.416 --> 12:39.457
Someone had to have altered
the blood test in the lab.

12:39.458 --> 12:41.833
I mean, who's gonna do that?

12:42.416 --> 12:44.040
Who would take my son?

12:44.041 --> 12:46.291
That's what David and I
have been trying to figure out.

12:47.916 --> 12:48.916
David.

12:49.958 --> 12:53.416
God, I said the most awful things to him
at the sentencing.

12:54.625 --> 12:56.333
- I mean, I thought…
- Hey, I know.

12:57.208 --> 12:58.958
But when I went to see him,

12:59.541 --> 13:01.541
you were the first thing he asked about.

13:02.416 --> 13:04.375
He wanted to make sure you were okay.

13:05.416 --> 13:07.583
When I told him you were remarried,

13:09.166 --> 13:10.833
he was genuinely happy for you.

13:11.416 --> 13:12.416
Really?

13:12.916 --> 13:14.750
I didn't mention it was to Ronald.

13:18.875 --> 13:20.916
If there's even a chance
that Matthew's out there,

13:21.500 --> 13:22.791
I need to do something.

13:23.625 --> 13:25.750
I'm not just gonna sit around and hope.

13:26.708 --> 13:28.000
It doesn't make sense.

13:28.708 --> 13:30.250
You gotta have him.

13:31.625 --> 13:33.332
You got Hilde Winslow to lie on the stand.

13:33.333 --> 13:34.957
Yeah, I did that.

13:34.958 --> 13:36.291
But that's all I did.

13:37.125 --> 13:40.790
After planting evidence
that sent my son to prison,

13:40.791 --> 13:44.750
your father turns around
and he hides evidence to try and save you.

13:45.250 --> 13:48.208
That's the kind of hypocrisy
I cannot let stand.

13:49.416 --> 13:53.540
But since it appears you might
be innocent, that changes things.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.624
So what now, Nicky?

13:55.625 --> 13:58.333
Well, now he's free to go.

14:01.833 --> 14:04.457
I hope you find your son. I truly do.

14:04.458 --> 14:05.625
You hope?

14:08.375 --> 14:09.833
What am I supposed to do now?

14:11.083 --> 14:13.708
How do I find the sick bastard
that took my son?

14:14.208 --> 14:15.541
Yeah, well,

14:16.458 --> 14:19.582
first, I'd be smart enough
not to make that assumption.

14:19.583 --> 14:20.958
You're missing the obvious.

14:22.166 --> 14:23.332
Which is?

14:23.333 --> 14:26.207
This isn't some pedo in a white panel van.

14:26.208 --> 14:28.290
This is planned.

14:28.291 --> 14:31.333
It's meticulous,
it's complicated, it's diabolical.

14:32.500 --> 14:35.999
He's right. Matthew was targeted.
You need to figure out why.

14:36.000 --> 14:38.124
There's no reason why they'd take my son.

14:38.125 --> 14:40.000
Yeah, there he goes again,
missing the obvious.

14:40.666 --> 14:41.957
Yeah, what's that?

14:41.958 --> 14:43.874
He's not just your son.

14:43.875 --> 14:45.833
He's Cheryl's son, as well.

14:46.416 --> 14:49.415
Look, you wanna figure out
who would do something this awful?

14:49.416 --> 14:54.083
Start asking yourself questions
that you obviously are afraid to ask.

14:55.041 --> 14:57.332
What happened in your past,

14:57.333 --> 14:59.124
in your wife's past,

14:59.125 --> 15:00.874
in your marriage,

15:00.875 --> 15:04.665
that would give someone
a reason to do something like this.

15:04.666 --> 15:05.750
Got it?

15:06.375 --> 15:10.332
'Cause I'm betting there's an explanation
that makes some kind of sense.

15:10.333 --> 15:12.666
Whether you're willing to admit it or not.

15:19.250 --> 15:21.166
Nicky hit on something, didn't he?

15:23.458 --> 15:24.458
What is it?

15:26.000 --> 15:27.999
I need to talk to Cheryl.

15:28.000 --> 15:29.958
Nicky's plane will take you back.

15:31.166 --> 15:32.791
You'll be in Boston in a few hours.

15:33.500 --> 15:34.958
I'll tell you on the flight.

15:35.958 --> 15:37.333
Lenny's not going with you.

15:38.458 --> 15:40.041
What are you talking about?

15:41.416 --> 15:42.458
Let me guess.

15:43.125 --> 15:46.916
Nicky needs an insurance policy
in case this all turns out to be bullshit.

15:49.208 --> 15:50.540
You gotta be kidding me.

15:50.541 --> 15:52.291
Just focus on what matters.

15:53.375 --> 15:55.291
Make sure nothing happens to him.

15:55.916 --> 15:57.166
Always.

15:57.875 --> 15:59.625
It's why I did what I did, David.

16:00.291 --> 16:01.750
To protect them.

16:04.291 --> 16:05.666
And if you see my father,

16:07.333 --> 16:08.540
just…

16:08.541 --> 16:09.500
Hey.

16:10.125 --> 16:11.291
Whatever it is,

16:12.166 --> 16:13.875
he needs to hear it from you.

16:15.625 --> 16:18.082
I mean, I pointed a gun
at Nicky Fisher's head.

16:18.083 --> 16:20.500
Generally, you don't get to do that
and wake up the next day.

16:22.958 --> 16:24.541
Just tell him I love him.

16:25.375 --> 16:26.416
Yeah, I will.

16:29.041 --> 16:30.916
Bring home my grandson.

16:51.333 --> 16:53.915
Hey, I got the photos. Thank you.

16:53.916 --> 16:55.374
You find anything yet?

16:55.375 --> 16:57.749
No, but I still have
a couple hundred more to go through.

16:57.750 --> 17:00.708
Well, I'm on my way over.
We can divide and conquer.

17:21.458 --> 17:24.374
You hungry? I can stop
and get something on the way.

17:24.375 --> 17:27.915
No, Cheryl was by earlier. She brought me
a Danish from Torretta's. How lucky am I?

17:27.916 --> 17:29.291
All right. I'll see you in a minute. Bye.

17:54.166 --> 17:57.666
Charlie 6-1, I have a Code 7
at Rachel Mills's home, and I need backup.

18:13.416 --> 18:14.833
Ms. Mills! BPD!

18:16.041 --> 18:17.583
He's got a gun!

18:30.500 --> 18:32.332
- What?
- Drive. Drive!

18:32.333 --> 18:33.833
Okay, okay!

18:40.875 --> 18:46.125
Rachel? Hey, what's happening?
Are you okay? Rachel. Rachel!

18:47.916 --> 18:51.124
I can't breathe. Pull over. Stop the car.

18:51.125 --> 18:52.666
Yeah, okay, okay.

19:11.166 --> 19:14.041
Hey, what happened?
What-- What just happened?

19:16.041 --> 19:17.333
You're okay.

19:18.333 --> 19:20.457
This guy just tried to kill me.

19:20.458 --> 19:21.416
What?

19:22.083 --> 19:25.040
This guy broke into my house and tried
to kill me, and then he shot a cop.

19:25.041 --> 19:27.665
- Someone shot a cop? What?
- Yeah, he just shot the cop.

19:27.666 --> 19:29.665
He shot a cop who was stationed out front.

19:29.666 --> 19:30.958
What?

19:31.666 --> 19:34.249
Wait, fuck, we have to go back.
We can't just stay here.

19:34.250 --> 19:36.582
- We can't go back. Rachel…
- I can't just leave him there.

19:36.583 --> 19:38.707
- No, we can't go back.
- He tried to help me.

19:38.708 --> 19:41.332
No, we have to call 911.
We can't go back there, okay?

19:41.333 --> 19:43.124
Look, we gotta get you on a plane.

19:43.125 --> 19:45.040
Don't worry about passports,
clothes, anything.

19:45.041 --> 19:47.708
- I can get you in the air in one hour.
- What?

19:48.500 --> 19:51.415
Whoever is coming after you,
whoever shot a cop,

19:51.416 --> 19:52.790
they are not going to stop.

19:52.791 --> 19:56.957
Whoever's behind all of this,
they are not going to stop.

19:56.958 --> 19:58.875
Rachel, you are being hunted.

20:04.041 --> 20:08.707
Look, I'm not asking you
to walk away from finding Matthew.

20:08.708 --> 20:12.416
Look, I'm asking you
to be smart about this.

20:13.458 --> 20:15.416
I can hire the best lawyers,

20:15.958 --> 20:20.874
the best investigators to find this person
and then to exonerate David.

20:20.875 --> 20:24.375
But none of this is gonna matter
if you are dead, okay?

20:26.541 --> 20:27.625
Do you understand?

20:29.708 --> 20:31.666
Come on. Let me keep you safe.

20:34.458 --> 20:35.707
And where would we go?

20:35.708 --> 20:36.916
Wherever you want.

20:38.083 --> 20:40.458
Listen, wherever you want to go.

20:41.333 --> 20:42.333
Okay?

20:44.750 --> 20:45.750
Okay?

20:47.875 --> 20:49.125
Come on.

21:01.000 --> 21:03.624
Hey, are you okay?

21:03.625 --> 21:04.874
Where are you?

21:04.875 --> 21:06.708
Hey, I'm on a plane back to Boston.

21:07.291 --> 21:08.999
On a plane?

21:09.000 --> 21:10.249
Back from where?

21:10.250 --> 21:12.290
I just met with Nicky Fisher.

21:12.291 --> 21:14.207
He doesn't have Matthew.

21:14.208 --> 21:15.790
- We had it all wrong.
- Jesus.

21:15.791 --> 21:18.582
- How can that be?
- There's something else.

21:18.583 --> 21:21.541
I'll be landing in Norwood
in about 20 minutes. I'll tell you then.

21:22.166 --> 21:24.458
Can you please just tell me
what's going on?

21:26.208 --> 21:27.916
Matthew may not be my son.

21:31.750 --> 21:33.124
All right.

21:33.125 --> 21:35.165
Cream, extra sugar,
if I remember correctly.

21:35.166 --> 21:38.582
Thanks. You'd think the FBI
would make better coffee.

21:38.583 --> 21:41.165
Oh, it's an old law enforcement tactic.

21:41.166 --> 21:44.791
See, nothing will get you talking faster
than burnt coffee in a Styrofoam cup.

21:45.375 --> 21:46.375
It worked.

21:48.166 --> 21:49.541
I told him, Philip.

21:50.458 --> 21:54.457
I told him I thought Nicky Fisher
took Lenny and that Matthew was alive.

21:54.458 --> 21:55.582
- Yeah.
- I just--

21:55.583 --> 21:57.499
You did the right thing.

21:57.500 --> 21:59.207
You did.

21:59.208 --> 22:03.000
Look, if Nicky has him, the FBI's
our best shot at getting him back, right?

22:04.291 --> 22:05.333
Hi, Sophie?

22:06.833 --> 22:07.999
Cheryl.

22:08.000 --> 22:10.625
Sorry for just, uh, dropping by like this.

22:11.458 --> 22:14.375
Oh, stop. You're always welcome here.

22:17.958 --> 22:19.333
Good to see you again.

22:20.000 --> 22:21.750
Rachel showed me the photo.

22:24.375 --> 22:25.958
It's him, right? It's…

22:26.833 --> 22:27.916
It's Matthew.

22:30.250 --> 22:34.165
I guess no one's gonna believe
any of this based on a photo.

22:34.166 --> 22:37.582
We need to prove the DNA test was altered.

22:37.583 --> 22:42.790
We need to prove that the boy they found
in Matthew's bed that night wasn't him.

22:42.791 --> 22:46.582
Well, the original sample of the blood
they found that night is in storage.

22:46.583 --> 22:49.832
We just need something
with Matthew's DNA to compare it to.

22:49.833 --> 22:53.541
You know, I have a friend at the lab
who can run it. Keep it off the books.

22:54.583 --> 22:55.958
From his first haircut.

23:03.875 --> 23:07.249
I thought, well,
I didn't think he'd sit still for it.

23:07.250 --> 23:09.708
I thought he was gonna squirm
and be a nightmare, but…

23:10.875 --> 23:12.208
he just sat there,

23:13.125 --> 23:14.916
smiling at me in the mirror.

23:16.250 --> 23:17.916
He was so proud of himself.

23:19.916 --> 23:21.458
If Matthew's out there,

23:22.416 --> 23:23.833
I need to find him.

23:32.625 --> 23:34.500
- How's your head?
- It's okay.

23:35.166 --> 23:38.708
And you were the first officer on scene,
Detective Stavros?

23:39.291 --> 23:42.290
That's right.
A Code 7 came across my scanner.

23:42.291 --> 23:43.915
Happened to be close.

23:43.916 --> 23:47.208
Door's open.
I draw my weapon, come into the house.

23:48.166 --> 23:49.957
And I find Officer Ramirez on the ground.

23:49.958 --> 23:52.083
I go to check his pulse,
and that's when he gets a jump on me.

23:52.666 --> 23:53.875
Who?

23:54.375 --> 23:55.875
David Burroughs.

23:59.916 --> 24:00.750
Hey.

24:03.916 --> 24:07.125
And you thought
my cholesterol was gonna kill me.

24:12.208 --> 24:13.458
I'm sorry, Dad.

24:14.708 --> 24:16.249
Kicking Skunk was my call.

24:16.250 --> 24:17.916
Don't beat yourself up.

24:19.583 --> 24:20.583
I mean,

24:21.208 --> 24:25.333
it did work, just not like
how we wanted it to, that's all.

24:28.041 --> 24:29.291
So what happened?

24:31.166 --> 24:34.666
The plane touched down in Miami,
and Burroughs wasn't on it.

24:36.791 --> 24:37.791
Not that.

24:39.125 --> 24:41.750
You know what I'm talking about.
What happened?

24:42.750 --> 24:44.458
Julie is benching me.

24:45.625 --> 24:48.332
And I'm pretty sure Seattle
is off the table.

24:48.333 --> 24:51.540
Oh, hell no, it ain't off the table.
Listen, tomorrow--

24:51.541 --> 24:54.540
Can we please not talk
about this right now, Dad?

24:54.541 --> 24:56.499
I don't wanna talk about Seattle.

24:56.500 --> 25:00.582
I don't really care about Seattle,
because honestly, I'm relieved.

25:00.583 --> 25:03.125
Relieved? Why?

25:03.708 --> 25:06.624
Because I probably
would never see you again.

25:06.625 --> 25:08.999
What the hell are you talking about?

25:09.000 --> 25:12.041
You and I are close now
because we're partners, but…

25:13.416 --> 25:16.375
what happens when
we don't see each other every day at work?

25:16.916 --> 25:20.457
How long until we're strangers again?
A couple holidays?

25:20.458 --> 25:21.333
Look,

25:22.041 --> 25:24.250
I don't have a time machine, okay?

25:24.958 --> 25:30.124
I can't change the past,
and I wish I could, but come on.

25:30.125 --> 25:32.749
I mean, you're being a little dramatic.

25:32.750 --> 25:36.958
We will never, ever be strangers
ever again.

25:37.750 --> 25:38.875
How do you know that?

25:42.625 --> 25:43.666
When…

25:45.250 --> 25:47.000
When I divorced your mother…

25:50.416 --> 25:52.791
you were the one that got hurt.

25:55.666 --> 25:58.250
And I hurt you, baby.
I hurt my little girl.

26:01.666 --> 26:03.375
And I know-- I know that.

26:04.583 --> 26:08.582
And I would rather have died on that table

26:08.583 --> 26:11.250
than to ever hurt you again.

26:12.875 --> 26:16.499
Us being partners
is giving us a second chance.

26:16.500 --> 26:19.999
Do you think that I wanna screw that up?
Are you crazy?

26:20.000 --> 26:24.415
So I don't care if it's Seattle or Spain,

26:24.416 --> 26:28.291
we are never
gonna be strangers ever again!

26:55.833 --> 26:58.249
What do you mean,
Matthew may not be your son?

26:58.250 --> 26:59.832
I don't know how much Cheryl told you,

26:59.833 --> 27:02.415
but when we decided to start a family,
we couldn't get pregnant.

27:02.416 --> 27:04.124
Yeah, I remember.

27:04.125 --> 27:07.040
Did she tell you
she looked into using a donor?

27:07.041 --> 27:08.457
She said she thought about it.

27:08.458 --> 27:10.583
She did more than think about it.

27:12.041 --> 27:14.458
She went to a fertility clinic
behind my back.

27:16.583 --> 27:17.499
Wait, what?

27:17.500 --> 27:20.666
And when I confronted her, she said it
was a consultation and that was it, but…

27:21.500 --> 27:25.791
I can't shake this feeling that maybe
she lied and she went through with it.

27:26.375 --> 27:29.458
No, I mean, no.
Cheryl wouldn't do something like that.

27:30.041 --> 27:31.165
You know her, Rachel.

27:31.166 --> 27:33.832
When it comes to Cheryl,
there's no problem that can't be solved.

27:33.833 --> 27:36.082
No, but not that.

27:36.083 --> 27:37.958
She always wanted to be a mom.

27:39.666 --> 27:44.208
So if not getting pregnant is the problem,
then maybe the donor is the solution.

27:48.125 --> 27:51.291
And you think the donor kidnapped Matthew?

27:51.916 --> 27:54.375
Yeah, he decided he wanted his kid back.

27:56.958 --> 27:59.333
It's the first explanation
that makes any sense.

28:06.083 --> 28:07.540
Thank you so much.

28:07.541 --> 28:08.583
Hey, Sarah.

28:09.500 --> 28:11.833
- What are you doing here?
- How's he doing?

28:12.458 --> 28:14.750
He's out of surgery. He's just resting.

28:15.416 --> 28:16.457
What is this?

28:16.458 --> 28:18.749
Got emailed to us
by a detective in Geneva.

28:18.750 --> 28:20.290
Concerns the Matthew Burroughs case.

28:20.291 --> 28:23.875
- Said you put out a request on Interpol.
- Julie benched me. Is she okay with this?

28:24.750 --> 28:26.125
I highly doubt it.

28:26.750 --> 28:28.000
Thanks, Chopra.

28:29.333 --> 28:30.999
Yeah, I don't know.

28:31.000 --> 28:32.957
I'm just as open-minded as the next guy,

28:32.958 --> 28:35.790
but this Müller,
I think he's spiking his hot chocolate.

28:35.791 --> 28:39.874
Look, if the body that night
was not Matthew Burroughs,

28:39.875 --> 28:41.332
it had to be someone.

28:41.333 --> 28:45.249
But how does a missing orphan from Geneva
end up beaten to death in Boston?

28:45.250 --> 28:48.040
…press conference
on the David Burroughs case.

28:48.041 --> 28:51.249
At 10:20 a.m.
on Westgate Avenue in Revere,

28:51.250 --> 28:56.833
Officer Danny Ramirez was shot and killed
inside the home of Rachel Mills.

28:57.416 --> 29:00.416
We now believe
the shooter was David Burroughs.

29:01.000 --> 29:04.041
If BPD finds Burroughs first,
he's a dead man.

29:06.041 --> 29:08.874
Lieutenant, tips are flooding in
about a black Range Rover

29:08.875 --> 29:10.582
that was spotted
leaving Rachel Mills' place

29:10.583 --> 29:11.832
around the time of the shooting.

29:11.833 --> 29:13.540
- Anyone get the license?
- Better.

29:13.541 --> 29:15.832
Neighbor's doorbell cam
picked them up as they passed.

29:15.833 --> 29:18.333
Vehicle is registered to a Hayden Payne.

29:21.833 --> 29:23.332
Okay, so what's the plan now?

29:23.333 --> 29:24.999
I gotta talk to Cheryl.

29:25.000 --> 29:27.040
No way. It's too dangerous.

29:27.041 --> 29:29.415
After this morning,
cops are gonna be all over her.

29:29.416 --> 29:30.457
What? What happened?

29:30.458 --> 29:33.457
A guy broke into my apartment
and tried to shoot me.

29:33.458 --> 29:36.082
- Do you know who?
- No, but the guy killed a cop.

29:36.083 --> 29:37.541
And the police think it was you.

29:38.666 --> 29:40.541
And even if what you're saying is true,

29:41.125 --> 29:43.458
she wouldn't know
the name of the donor, right?

29:44.208 --> 29:46.000
The fertility clinic would.

29:46.833 --> 29:48.375
Okay, do you remember which one?

29:48.958 --> 29:50.290
Berg.

29:50.291 --> 29:51.625
Berg Reproductive?

29:52.208 --> 29:53.041
That's it.

29:53.833 --> 29:55.625
They're a part of Payne Medical Group.

29:56.208 --> 29:57.790
Any chance you can get us the file?

29:57.791 --> 29:59.666
Yeah, I think I can.

30:17.958 --> 30:20.790
Thanks, Pam. 1-1-3-4.

30:20.791 --> 30:23.665
No, no, I just gotta get some paperwork
for the board meeting.

30:23.666 --> 30:26.125
- Thank you so much. Okay, bye.
- You sure no one will be here?

30:26.708 --> 30:28.041
Yeah, it's the weekend.

30:28.625 --> 30:30.208
My first B&E.

30:30.916 --> 30:33.916
It's not breaking and entering
if you own the building.

30:35.500 --> 30:36.625
Fair enough.

30:39.291 --> 30:41.083
Come on. It's this way.

30:54.791 --> 30:57.790
- Cheryl doesn't have a file.
- That doesn't make any sense.

30:57.791 --> 30:59.790
She came here.
How can she not have a file?

30:59.791 --> 31:01.541
Try using her maiden name.

31:03.833 --> 31:05.332
Nope.

31:05.333 --> 31:08.582
Maybe the donor was able
to erase it somehow, cover his tracks.

31:08.583 --> 31:11.290
Unless you work for Berg,
how is that even possible?

31:11.291 --> 31:12.874
Holy shit.

31:12.875 --> 31:14.124
Wait, hold on a second.

31:14.125 --> 31:16.999
Five years ago,
Berg fired a doctor who they suspected

31:17.000 --> 31:20.832
was impregnating his patients
with his own donations.

31:20.833 --> 31:22.165
- What?
- Yeah.

31:22.166 --> 31:23.207
What's his name?

31:23.208 --> 31:25.082
Heller. Dr. Jacob Heller.

31:25.083 --> 31:27.582
A fertility doctor
impregnating his own patients.

31:27.583 --> 31:29.833
How is that not front page of the news?

31:31.500 --> 31:33.083
Your mother covered it up.

31:33.875 --> 31:34.958
Yeah.

31:35.541 --> 31:37.249
Had Heller step down,

31:37.250 --> 31:39.457
made everybody sign NDAs.

31:39.458 --> 31:42.290
She's nothing if not thorough.

31:42.291 --> 31:44.457
Well, we gotta find Heller.
You know where he is?

31:44.458 --> 31:46.500
- No.
- Wait, you guys, I found him.

31:48.208 --> 31:49.874
Dr. Jacob Heller.

31:49.875 --> 31:53.000
He works at Boston General with Cheryl.

31:54.208 --> 31:55.374
Dr. Dreason.

31:55.375 --> 31:57.540
Cheryl, did you know
there's a police officer

31:57.541 --> 31:59.207
stationed outside your office?

31:59.208 --> 32:00.875
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

32:01.375 --> 32:03.040
Sorry, I gotta prep for CDH.

32:03.041 --> 32:05.750
- You sure everything's okay?
- Yeah, everything's fine.

32:12.625 --> 32:15.874
- We gotta get to the hospital.
- How? There's gonna be cops everywhere.

32:15.875 --> 32:17.707
Speaking of.

32:17.708 --> 32:19.207
- Shit.
- We gotta go.

32:19.208 --> 32:20.540
How did they find us?

32:20.541 --> 32:22.416
I don't know,
but we gotta get out of here.

32:23.958 --> 32:26.291
There's a back door
that leads to an alleyway, okay?

32:28.750 --> 32:30.958
- I'll buy you guys some time.
- Hayden.

32:31.541 --> 32:33.000
Go! Rachel, go!

32:34.416 --> 32:35.458
Go.

32:40.875 --> 32:44.416
Stop! Hands in the air!
Move towards us slowly!

32:49.333 --> 32:51.750
Lay down! Flat on the ground!

32:52.625 --> 32:54.166
Hands behind your head!

32:55.541 --> 32:57.333
Move in. Look for Burroughs.

33:07.458 --> 33:08.583
Jesus.

33:10.708 --> 33:12.333
What are you doing here?

33:15.166 --> 33:17.166
She can no longer protect you.

33:18.166 --> 33:19.583
You need to leave.

33:20.500 --> 33:21.458
Now.
